Title: Comparative Cardiovascular Safety and Exploratory Bleeding Outcomes of Ibrutinib, Acalabrutinib, and Zanubrutinib in Mantle Cell Lymphoma: A Propensity Score-Matched Real-World Analysis.
Abstract: Bruton tyrosine kinase inhibitors are central to the treatment of relapsed or refractory mantle cell lymphoma, but cardiovascular and bleeding toxicities influence treatment selection. Ibrutinib has been associated with atrial fibrillation/flutter and other cardiovascular adverse events, whereas second-generation covalent BTK inhibitors were developed to improve kinase selectivity and tolerability. Mantle cell lymphoma-specific real-world comparative safety data across ibrutinib, acalabrutinib, and zanubrutinib remain limited.

